Melbourne road repairs: which come first

Data in data/ is derived from:
- Road segments with surface type, road corridors, and landmarks and places of interest (health services):
  City of Melbourne Open Data, licensed under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
- School locations 2026: Victorian Department of Education, DataVic, licensed under CC BY 4.0.

The derived data is released under CC BY 4.0 (LICENSE-DATA), with these credits kept.
The notebook and code are released under the MIT licence (LICENSE).

data/sample_inspection.csv is a made-up sample to show the inspection workflow. It is not real inspection data.
Unit rates are typical published council rates (Knox City Council, Wodonga, Warrnambool asset management plans);
costs are indicative, not quotes.

This is independent work using open data, not endorsed by the City of Melbourne or the Victorian Government.
Base maps in visuals/: (c) OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL), tiles Protomaps.

POWER BI MAP CONTEXT
  The Shape Map in powerbi/ draws suburb and locality boundaries and the City of Melbourne boundary round the
  segments: Australian Bureau of Statistics, ASGS Edition 3, Suburbs and Localities 2021, Local Government Areas 2021
  and Mesh Blocks 2021 (water), CC BY 4.0; with the river and harbour cut out of them from Vicmap Hydro water areas,
  State of Victoria (Department of Transport and Planning), CC BY 4.0. The faint road outlines are the rated segments
  themselves (City of Melbourne, CC BY 4.0). All generalised and cut to the map frame. Water itself is the map
  background showing where no land is drawn.

